---
import LegalPage from '@shared/components/LegalPage.astro';
import { bronzed } from '@shared/data/apps';
---

<LegalPage
  app={bronzed}
  kind="Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy Policy for the Bronzed app by Camm Studios."
  updated="June 25, 2026"
>
  <p>
    This Privacy Policy applies specifically to the <strong>Bronzed - Tan Timer &amp; UV Index</strong>
    app ("Bronzed") developed by Camm Studios. This supplements our
    <a href="https://www.cammstudios.com/privacy">general Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>1. What Data Bronzed Stores Locally</h2>
  <p>
    All of the following data is stored <strong>locally on your device only</strong> and never
    transmitted to our servers:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your Fitzpatrick skin type and how your skin reacts to the sun</li>
    <li>Your current and goal tan shade</li>
    <li>Default SPF, temperature units, and vitamin D goal</li>
    <li>Your tanning session history (duration, UV index, SPF used, estimated vitamin D, weather conditions)</li>
    <li>Streaks and progress data</li>
    <li>Notification preferences</li>
    <li>Onboarding completion status</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not have access to any of this data. It never leaves your device.</p>

  <h2>2. Location and Weather Data</h2>
  <p>
    With your permission, Bronzed uses your device location ("when in use") to provide accurate,
    local sun information. Your location is used to:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Fetch the current UV index, temperature, and forecast from <strong>Apple WeatherKit</strong></li>
    <li>Search for and display place names via <strong>Apple MapKit</strong> when you choose a custom location</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Your location is processed by Apple to return weather data and is handled under
    <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/" rel="noopener">Apple's Privacy Policy</a>. Camm
    Studios does <strong>not</strong> store your precise location on our servers or use it for
    advertising. You can use the app without granting location access by entering a location
    manually.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Notifications</h2>
  <p>
    If you enable notifications, Bronzed schedules local reminders on your device (such as a
    heads-up to flip during a session, a daily check-in, and a reminder before your free trial
    ends). These are processed entirely by iOS and do not involve any external servers.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Analytics and Usage Data</h2>
  <p>
    Bronzed uses <strong>PostHog</strong> for analytics. The following anonymous usage events are
    collected to help us understand how the app is used and improve it:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Screen views:</strong> Which screens you visit (Home, Tanning, Profile, Settings, SPF Guide, Tips, Vitamin D)</li>
    <li><strong>Onboarding events:</strong> Steps viewed and completion, including the skin type, shade, and SPF you select</li>
    <li><strong>Session events:</strong> Starting, pausing, completing, or ending a tanning session, with the skin type, UV index, SPF, and duration</li>
    <li><strong>Settings changes:</strong> Skin type, default SPF, units, and notification preferences</li>
    <li><strong>Subscription events:</strong> Paywall views, purchase starts, completions, cancellations, and restores</li>
    <li><strong>App lifecycle:</strong> App installs, opens, and session data</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    PostHog does <strong>not</strong> receive your name, email, or precise location. Analytics data
    is sent to PostHog's servers in the United States.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Subscription Data</h2>
  <p>
    Your subscription is managed through Apple's App Store and <strong>RevenueCat</strong>. We do
    not receive your name, email, or payment details.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>RevenueCat</strong> receives: an anonymous user identifier, purchase receipts, and subscription status, used to unlock premium access and restore purchases</li>
    <li><strong>RevenueCat does not receive:</strong> your email, location, or session content</li>
    <li><strong>Apple App Store:</strong> Processes all billing and payments directly</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. Health-Related Information</h2>
  <p>
    Bronzed uses your skin type and tanning history to estimate safe sun-exposure times and tailor
    your routine. This information is treated as described above (stored locally, with anonymous
    analytics) and is <strong>not</strong> sold or shared with advertisers. Bronzed is not a medical
    device and does not collect data through Apple Health.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Data Deletion</h2>
  <p>
    To delete all your locally stored Bronzed data, simply delete the app from your device. This
    permanently removes all content stored on your device.
  </p>
  <p>
    To request deletion of analytics data held by our third-party providers (PostHog and
    RevenueCat), contact us at the email below and we will process your request.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Your Privacy Rights</h2>

  <h3>European Economic Area (GDPR)</h3>
  <p>
    If you are in the EEA, you have the right to access, correct, delete, restrict processing, and
    port your personal data. You may also withdraw consent at any time. Contact us to exercise
    these rights.
  </p>

  <h3>California Residents (CCPA)</h3>
  <p>
    California residents have the right to know what data is collected, request deletion, and opt
    out of data sales. We do not sell your personal information. Contact us to exercise these
    rights.
  </p>

  <h3>Australian Users (Privacy Act 1988)</h3>
  <p>
    Australian users have the right to access and correct personal information under the Australian
    Privacy Principles. Contact us to make a request.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about Bronzed's privacy practices or want to exercise your privacy rights? Email us at
    <a href="mailto:info@cammstudios.com">info@cammstudios.com</a>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
